/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Let gas at absolute pressure p push a piston of area A through a small distance dx.
   - W₁₂ is the work done by the system in kJ; p is absolute pressure in kPa; V is volume in m³ (1 kPa × 1 m³ = 1 kJ).
   - Expansion (V₂ > V₁) gives positive work, done by the gas; compression gives negative work, done on the gas.
   - For the polytropic path, p₂ = p₁(V₁/V₂)ⁿ.
   - In a free expansion, gas rushes from a tank into an evacuated space.
   - Each mode is a generalised force times the change of a generalised displacement.
   - Paddle-wheel (stirring) work is shaft work done on a fluid; it can only enter the fluid, never come back out as shaft work.
*/
